  "notes": "Drawn from the 737-8 MAX N47275 (left, Apr 2025), checked on the A321neo N24513 (Aug 2026). The belly is in shadow in both photos: its gray is from United's description, the navy line's path from the photos. The globe's lines aren't traced. Many aircraft still fly the 2010 scheme (gold line, gold globe): see standard-2010. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on the 737-8 MAX (same fuselage as the 737-800, so on the measured 737-800 shape): two photos (N47275, N17306) fitted with the doors and windows pinned agree the navy line runs 0.1-0.25 lower than first drawn (it crosses the aft door's lower part about 0.25 m above its sill, and runs about 0.4 m under the forward door's sill) and dips to about y -0.44 behind the wing; the title runs x 0.179-0.445, its baseline about 0.2 m under the windows' bottom. On the longer 737-900ER and MAX 9 (and the A321neo) the same 10 m title covers a smaller share. The title's face measured 2026-11-20 on N47275 (each face set as the title, its letter outlines against the photo's): Helvetica Neue Bold follows the letters closely, Open Sans ExtraBold's run narrower, so Helvetica comes first. The globe mark redrawn 2026-11-27 (our own drawing of a sphere's latitude lines and meridian bars, checked on N19141, N77571 and the right side of N37556); its lines are in the fin blue. The fin's halftone darkening toward the tip isn't drawn.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximate standard (a few colors from memory). The 2019 'Evo Blue' livery replaced the 2010 post-merger scheme (Continental's colors with United titles); repainting is gradual, so both fly."
}
